{"Component exported from BackupCode.tsx is named TwoFactor instead of BackupCode, making DevTools, stack traces, and search results point to the wrong component during auth debugging": 0.7321351766586304, "Backup code validation reads full plaintext list, checks in memory, then writes back updated encrypted array - this leaves backup codes recoverable at rest and opens a TOCTOU window where two parallel requests can both pass the lookup before either write null": 0.6557865142822266, "locator.isChecked() returns a Promise<boolean>, so expect(locator.isChecked()).toBeTruthy() only asserts that a Promise object exists, not its resolved value - should use data-state attribute check instead": 0.1514965444803238, "Migration timestamp 20230804153419 is older than existing migrations like 20230828094603, causing Prisma migration-order drift across environments": 0.41986578702926636, "Password visibility toggle button has tabIndex={-1} which removes it from keyboard navigation, causing accessibility regression for keyboard-only users": 0.8586707711219788, "SSO users still can't authenticate with backup codes because guards only exempt totpCode - a Google/SAML user submitting backupCode will hit ThirdPartyIdentityProviderEnabled or IncorrectEmailPassword before the backup-code branch runs": 0.9733799695968628, "When totpEmail is present the login page switches to ExternalTotpFooter, so SAML/Google users never see the new backup-code entry point and can still be locked out after losing their authenticator": 0.8890069127082825, "Test suite doesn't cover login-with-backup-code, disable-via-backup-code, or sequential reuse failure, so the recovery path can regress without CI noticing": 0.5552489757537842}